The Go rendering: a command that decodes documents through a YAML decoder it
makes refuse unknown keys inside a function that hands its parameter on, a JSON
decoder it makes refuse unknown members, a gob decoder, which has no such switch, a
YAML decoder whose switch it turns off, a second YAML decoder that takes no switch,
sigs.k8s.io/yaml given its strict option and a goccy YAML decoder made with its
strict option, an encoding/json/v2 decode whose strict option takes a flag the
command computes, a YAML v2 decoder whose switch it sets through a method value,
and a go.yaml.in YAML v2 decoder whose switch it sets through a method expression.
The five YAML packages are local modules the target requires and replaces, so the
rendering loads with no network access.

